# What `project/adopted.py` and `project/sail_adoption.py` rendered before the standing text in them
# moved out to `assets/`, as SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of each page and each appended block.
#
# The move is only worth doing if it changed nothing a repository receives, and "generate before and
# after" cannot be run across one commit. So these were captured at a6a0aed, the commit slice 16.6 was
# written on top of, by the matrix `tests/adopted_pages.py` describes, and the new path has to reproduce
# them exactly. Anyone can take the same reading: check out a6a0aed, put that module beside this file, and
#
#     PYTHONPATH=src:tests python3 tests/adopted_pages.py
#
# and compare it with the lines below. The module that prints them changes nothing the generator does, so
# the reading is the same whether it is taken at a6a0aed or at the commit that added it.
#
# Six repositories: each of the five forges that can run the gate, each of the four paths a change takes
# to production, a repository that had a `Makefile` and one that had none, both delivery layouts, one that
# has converged, a language the keel generates beside one it does not, an adoption with nothing wrapped at
# all, and each home the schema and the infrastructure can be recorded at.
#
# The command pages these modules also reach — `commands/sail.md`, whose ladder gains the adoption's three
# stages — are in `command-pages.sha256` already and are deliberately not recorded twice.
#
# `<digest>  <repository>  <path>`. A `#` in a path marks a block appended to a file of the repository's
# own rather than a file the keel writes whole.
